import{H as e,at as t,it as n,vt as r}from"./chunks/framework.dmHZ7NHG.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"The field domain","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"params":{"slug":"electromagnetism","address":"1c780ce0-a916-8786-8ecb-ba2ee94ee759","receipt":"4f1e6d03-ab98-8297-9929-67117d67e1c7"},"relativePath":"docs/publications/electromagnetism.md","filePath":"docs/publications/[slug].md"}`),a={name:`docs/publications/electromagnetism.md`};function o(e,i,a,o,s,c){return r(),n(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="the-field-domain" tabindex="-1">The field domain <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-field-domain" aria-label="Permalink to “The field domain”">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>electromagnetism as decidable arithmetic, demarcated — Coulomb sets the sign (like repel, opposite attract), Ohm&#39;s law V=I·R, power V·I=I²R, series resistance adds and parallel combines reciprocally, Kirchhoff conserves current at a node and voltage around a loop, and Faraday induces EMF only from a changing flux — circuit and field arithmetic, not a full Maxwell derivation, distinct from the light waves in Optics</p></blockquote><p>These 8 facts hold by decision. Each was proven in Lean 4 — no Mathlib, checked sorry-free — and every sentence below links the proof that seals it. This note claims nothing beyond what its theorems settle: not that the domain is complete, only that the prose says nothing the proofs do not. It was written by reading the sealed ledger; read the proofs, not the prose.</p><h2 id="the-facts-each-backed-by-its-proof" tabindex="-1">The facts, each backed by its proof <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-facts-each-backed-by-its-proof" aria-label="Permalink to “The facts, each backed by its proof”">​</a></h2><ul><li>Coulomb&#39;s law sets the sign of the force by the product of charges: like charges (product &gt; 0) repel, opposite charges (product &lt; 0) attract — 1·1 &gt; 0 and 1·(−1) &lt; 0. Same sign pushes apart, opposite pulls together. — <a href="/theorem/coulomb_sign">proof</a>.</li><li>Ohm&#39;s law: the voltage across a resistor is the current times the resistance, V = I·R — 12 V = 2 A · 6 Ω. Push (voltage) equals flow times friction. — <a href="/theorem/ohms_law">proof</a>.</li><li>Electric power is voltage times current, and equally I²R: P = V·I = 12·2 = 24 W, and P = I²R = 2²·6 = 24 W. Two routes to the same dissipated power. — <a href="/theorem/electric_power">proof</a>.</li><li>Resistances in series add: current passes through each in turn, so R = R₁ + R₂ = 3 + 6 = 9 Ω. More resistors in a row, more resistance. — <a href="/theorem/series_resistance_adds">proof</a>.</li><li>Resistances in parallel combine reciprocally (1/R = 1/R₁ + 1/R₂): two 6 Ω resistors give 3 Ω, since R·(R₁+R₂) = R₁·R₂ — 3·(6+6) = 6·6 = 36. Another path lowers the total. — <a href="/theorem/parallel_resistance">proof</a>.</li><li>Kirchhoff&#39;s current law conserves charge at a node: what flows in flows out — 5 A in = 2 A + 3 A out. A junction stores no charge. — <a href="/theorem/kirchhoff_current">proof</a>.</li><li>Kirchhoff&#39;s voltage law: the voltages around a closed loop sum to zero — a 12 V source spent across 4 V and 8 V drops leaves 12 − 4 − 8 = 0. Energy per charge returns to where it started. — <a href="/theorem/kirchhoff_voltage">proof</a>.</li><li>Faraday&#39;s law induces EMF only from a CHANGING magnetic flux (EMF = −dΦ/dt): a constant flux induces nothing — 5 − 5 = 0. No change, no current; it is the change that drives induction. — <a href="/theorem/faraday_needs_changing_flux">proof</a>.</li></ul><h2 id="provenance" tabindex="-1">Provenance <a class="header-anchor" href="#provenance" aria-label="Permalink to “Provenance”">​</a></h2><p>These 8 proofs fold, order-invariant, to the receipt <code>4f1e6d03-ab98-8297-9929-67117d67e1c7</code> — recompute it from the same ledger and it returns. The note itself content-addresses to a uuid, so any edit is visible. Writing descends from reading: this note holds only what the proofs it links already sealed, and it was audited by uuidna&#39;s own honesty gate before it was published — a sentence that overreached a proof would have been refused, not shipped.</p><p>Source · <a href="https://github.com/uuidna/uuidna/blob/main/lean/Electromagnetism.lean" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">lean/Electromagnetism.lean</a> · <a href="/theorems">all theorems</a></p><hr><p><strong>Audited before published</strong> · this note passed uuidna&#39;s honesty gate at build time — every claim above links the proof that seals it. Content-address <code>1c780ce0</code> · proofs fold to receipt <code>4f1e6d03</code> (the handles; the full uuids are in this page&#39;s meta, recomputable) · 8 sealed theorems.</p><p><a href="/publications">All publications</a> · <a href="/theorems">All theorems</a> · <a href="/trials">How auditing works</a></p>`,11)]])}var s=e(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};